# Round mimog2's card: MiMo-V2.6-Flash MXFP4 prompt at the serving defaults on plan (a), the A6000 alone, with the prompt
# group the row's default (2: two batches in flight, the seat's) against groups of one (BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP=1), one
# binary, both writing the same bits (gate_mimo2_e2e clause (b), both groups and a call of three batches).
# Decomposition [derived, from promptcost's paper round and the gate logs of 2026-10-13]. A prompt of P ids is cut into
# ceil(P / 512) near-equal batches (runtime::prompt::batches, T_MAX 512), each walked layer by layer: 47 routed layers
# (layer 0 is dense), 256 experts a layer. promptcost's run, 5,620 ids = 11 batches, 53.9 s to the first token (104 tok/s),
# is 517 layer-batches x 102.4 ms + 0.96 s fixed (the dense layer, the head, the uploads) [derived: 11 x 47 = 517;
# 53.9 - 517 x 0.1024 = 0.96]. Per layer-batch the resources are, in ms (promptcost's figures):
#   host cores  the routed-expert union 66..75: 229.5 host experts a layer at 13.37 MB (3 x 4,096 x 2,048 x 17/32) is
#               3.08 GB, so 41..47 GB/s, a third of the 130..145 GB/s the decode leg reads (docs/cards/mimo2-r5.card):
#               compute-bound on the MXFP4 tile, not DRAM-bound [derived]
#   host DRAM   3.08 GB at ~140 GB/s = ~22 busy, under the union
#   card SMs    the attention front 27..35 (the card experts' shadow runs under the union)
#   PCIe        8.4 MB rows down + 8.4 MB sums up + 33 KB ids and weights at 12..26 GB/s: 0.65..1.4 in all
#   NVMe        0 (the host set is resident, plan (a) has no tier)
# Group of one: the walk is serial (front, download, union, upload and back), so the wall is the SUM, 27..35 + 66..75 + ~1
# = 94..111, the 102.4 measured. Group of two: layer-batch x's host serve runs under layer-batch x+1's card front
# (runtime::sched's batch order), so the wall is the MAX, the union, plus the join's exposed upload and back, e <= 3 ms: the
# card front, 27..35 ms, is under the host's shadow and worth 0 after this flow change. The flow lever (asynchrony across two
# batches) comes before any term is shortened: the front's GEMM lift or a faster front would predict 0 at group 2, and the
# union's tile rate is the bound that remains (a bulk union over a group's batches does not cut a compute-bound term).
# At P = 4096: 8 batches, 4 groups of 2, 376 layer-batches. Group of one 376 x 102.4 + 0.96 = 39.5 s, pp 103.7 tok/s.
# Group of two 376 x (66..75) + 0.96 = 25.8..29.2 s, pp 140..159, centre 150: effect (g2 - g1)/g1 = +35..+53 %. The
# lead's band, pp 142..158 against 104, is +37..+52 % and sits inside it (a union of 66.3..74.1 ms, e = 0); it is the card's.
# Its wall is -27..-34 % (-26..-35 % on the arithmetic above); the spec's "-28..-38 %" does not convert from its own pp band. The first token at 5,620 ids (517 layer-batches): 517 x (66..75) + 0.96 = 35.1..39.7 s
# against 53.9 s, the lead's 35.5..40; that is a second term, read only when the sitting raises DEPTH_SERVE_CTX to 5,760 for
# every arm (the ids file must hold 5,620; the plan, and so the card experts, move by 27 experts of ~3,100 with 1,600
# positions more of stores, under 1 %) and adds the D = 5620 arms: its rows are D = 5620's own table, never compared with
# D = 4096's. A prompt of one batch (P <= 512) is one group of one: pp @ 512 predicts 0 and is not run.
# The 102.4 ms split is not recorded: the MiMo seat does not act on BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS (it is not in its ACTS_ON, so the
# server refuses it by name) and gpu-mimo2's prefill carries no prompt timing (GLM's pattern is set_prompt_stats /
# take_prompt_stats with `stat prompt lb` and `stat prompt split`, whose fields union_ms, serve_ms, card_front_ms,
# card_down_ms, card_shadow_ms, card_upload_ms and card_back_ms would carry it). The pair of rates reads both terms
# instead: with r1 and r2 the pp of the two arms, lb_g = (4096 / r_g - 0.96) / 376 s a layer-batch, the union is ~lb_2 and
# the front lb_1 - lb_2. The smallest addition for a recorded split: MiMo's set/take_prompt_stats beside the existing
# `stat prompt` kinds, STEP_STATS in the seat's ACTS_ON and the seat's `Seat::step_stats`; not built here.
# One more risk, named: the MiMo plan reserves no card bytes for the prompt batch, so the default group's two extra units
# come out of the card's margin. The unit is 2 x 512 x 4,096 x 4 + 2 x 512 x 4 = 16,781,312 B [derived: UnitBufs::planned],
# so group 2 holds 2 units more than group 1: 33,562,624 B, against the batch's 316,919,808 B at group 1 (gate log
# 2026-10-13, measured); the plan's own margin is 1,024 MiB (mimo2-r5.card). A load the card cannot hold refuses by name
# with its free bytes. The two arms' `load` records are read for it: resident_bytes should differ by that 33,562,624 B.
# Sitting [the lead's]: one lease, 3 rounds, two arms, six fresh servers. Per server DEPTH_SERVE_LOAD_EST 41 s (the lead's
# figure; the gate logs of 2026-10-13 read 15.7..18.7 s to listening with the host set warm) + 5 s runner overhead + the
# request: 39.5 s at group 1, 25.8..29.2 s at group 2. A round is 2 x 46 + 39.5 + 27.5 = 159 s with the 41 s load, 111 s
# with a 17 s one: 3 rounds 5.5..8 min [derived], plus the recipe's own build of bloomery-serve in the tree (outside the
# lease) and the host set's page cache warm (a row marked [cold] is void). Run BLOOMERY_DRY=1 on the exact command first.
# GLM's priced term, for the same sitting [derived, not a card of its own: it takes the lease and so needs one]: the
# stats run of promptcost, one ours arm at P = 4096, plan (b'), a process of WARMUP r0 and two rounds (the runner's
# default), so three processes: each a load 51.9 s (the glm5next e2e-long gate's load at the gate plan, ctx 3,136, a proxy:
# the batch log of 2026-10-13, not this plan's) + the prompt 4096 / 172 tok/s = 23.8 s (promptcost's bp rate at 5,548 ids)
# + 2 decode steps + ~5 s runner overhead = ~81 s: three of them 4.1 min, 4..5 min with the host set's preheat. Command:
#   BLOOMERY_REMOTE='~/repo/bloomery-<tree>' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090
#   BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE=bp BLOOMERY_DECODE_N=3 BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/<its>.card'
#   just depth-gpu-glm5next 4096
# Its records are GLM's `stat prompt lb` (per layer-batch) and `stat prompt split` (summed) with the fields above.
kind: ab
question: does MiMo-V2.6-Flash's prompt at 4,096 ids run faster with two batches in flight (the row's default group) than
  with groups of one, by the card front the host union's shadow now hides?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096 prose ids (first 4,096 of the model's corpus-prose.ids), n_predict 2, ctx 4160, plan (a), A6000
  alone (the 3090 idle), bloomery-serve --model mimo2 at the serving defaults, group 2 (the lever unset) against
  BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP=1, same binary, paired by round: the runner's arm minus first arm, in percent
unit: %
predict: +37..+52
rounds: 3
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, per-round pp ratios of two binaries' prompt windows, the larger of the two runs'
  SD (carried from docs/cards/b1-pp.card, not re-derived for MiMo)
condition: one lease, one binary from the tree bloomery-mimog2, the arms in this order, so the first is the base and + is the
  default arm faster: BLOOMERY_REMOTE='~/repo/bloomery-mimog2' BLOOMERY_MODEL=mimo2 BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='DEPTH_SERVE_N=2 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/m2-group2-pp.card' just depth-serve
  env=BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP=1:bloomery-mimog2:4096 bloomery-mimog2:4096. Each arm's server log (the runner's LOGDIR
  r<k>-<label>-D4096.log) holds a `load` record with group=1 for the lever arm and group=2 for the bare arm, the same
  `plan` record card_experts in both arms (the plan reserves nothing for the units); no refusal naming free bytes; a row
  marked [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] is void; the witness blocks show no Xid; BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS is not set (the
  seat refuses it)
decide-in: group 2 pays as derived: the default stays; read lb_1 and lb_2 from the two rates and write the union and front
  into the MiMo model table; the first token at 5.6K (the D = 5620 arms at DEPTH_SERVE_CTX 5760) goes in the README's MiMo
  row; the next prompt term is the host union's tile rate (it is now the wall)
decide-below: below +37 the host union runs slower with two batches in flight than alone (the enqueue thread shares the
  cores) or the join exposes more than 3 ms: between +20 and +37 add MiMo's prompt timing (set/take_prompt_stats, STEP_STATS
  in the seat) and read union_ms and card_back_ms per layer-batch at group 2 before the default is judged; below +20 or a
  lower bound under +10 revert the default to 1 (the lever and the group path stay)
decide-above: above +52 the front is larger than 35 ms or the group-of-one union under 66 ms: re-derive u and f from the two
  rates (f = lb_1 - lb_2) before the front's GEMM lift opens, since the front is then the larger share and its lift has
  a band of its own
